  "text": "Solution 3 is the most carefully argued of the three, but I can't verify it, so my confidence is low.\n\n- **Solution 1 (24)** gives no derivation. It asserts the two values have equal magnitude and opposite sign, which is not checked.\n- **Solution 2 (3)** quotes a formula for ν̄ in terms of η-invariants and a Mathai–Quillen term, then asserts that all (k,l)-dependence cancels. I can't confirm that formula or the cancellation, and the result is asserted rather than derived.\n- **Solution 3 (6)** makes checkable claims. The flag-manifold disc bundle W has χ(W) = χ(F) = 6, which is correct since W deformation retracts to F. The intersection form on H⁴(W,∂W) has rank 2 and negative determinant, so σ(W) = 0. Its parity check is also consistent: the semi-characteristic 1+0+1+0 is even. The weak points are the assumption that the nearly-parallel structure extends over W as a Spin(7)-structure without zeros, and the step from ν ≡ 6 (mod 48) to the integer ν̄ = ±6. I could not confirm either from memory of the Crowley–Goette–Nordström paper.\n\nSince I can't establish any of the three values from first principles, I'm choosing the one whose reasoning holds up under inspection.\n\nCHOICE: 3",
